# Notebooks go into git WITHOUT their outputs: code and prose are versioned, figures are not.
# The stripping is done by tools/nb_strip_outputs.py, wired in as a "clean" filter. The filter
# itself is defined in .git/config, which is machine-local and not committed, so a fresh clone
# has to run tools/install_nb_filter.sh once before notebooks are stripped on commit.
#
# Your working copy keeps every figure. Only what git STORES is stripped.
*.ipynb filter=nbstrip text eol=lf
#
# THE ONE TRAP: git now hands back notebooks without outputs. Editing and committing is safe,
# but anything that REWRITES a notebook in your working tree -- `git checkout <file>`,
# `git stash`, a pull or merge that touches it -- replaces it with the stripped version, and
# the figures you had locally are gone until you re-run the notebook. Nothing in git is lost;
# the figures simply were never in there. Outputs committed before 2026-11-04 are still in
# history: `git show 3541da5:first_pass_analysis.ipynb`.
